{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/768447-ww2-wheres-the-other-pantheons","id":768447,"title":"WW2 Wheres the other pantheons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T06:08:33-08:00","id":768447,"title":"WW2 Wheres the other pantheons?","content":"Any ideas what the other pantheons, the Atzlanti, the Pesedjit, and Loa are doing during WW2? I cant see them just twiddling their thumbs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T10:53:18-08:00","id":768602,"title":"","content":"Apart from the fact that I think the WW2-campaign is a whole lot of balloney, I'd see them somewhere around these parts: <br /> <br /> Pesedjet: Staying in Africa and trying to make Erwin Rommel and the others back off. Even though they have Set on their side, of course, this will prove difficult as modern technology is not something they can counter that easily. Even Thot needs a bit of time to understand this technology and how to foil it. So there might be a lot of espionage going on from the Egyptian gods, but on the whole I don't see them getting into international quarrels as much as them simply protecting their (relatively small) turf. <br /> <br /> Dodekatheon: They pretty much twiddled their thumbs there or the whole war would have gone a lot differently than it did. Its not like Germany attacked them out of the blue, after all. Maybe they just underestimated the oncoming war and got struck dumb by it once it came to them. Not that uncommon amongst big tiers. <br /> <br /> Loa: A mixture of Pesedjet and Yankees: Indifferent at first and only willing to protect their turf (seeing as many of them were originally African Gods) but a whole lot more aggressive once things got.. lets say personal. All in all though I don't see them as a very active &quot;War-Pantheon&quot; at least when it comes to the Big Picture. They have, and always will be, focused on smaller scales of happenings. Who cares if theres a big war if your neighborhood is sufficiently fed and away from it? <br /> <br /> Azlanti: Just for the hell of it, they might have participated, but I'd sort them in a similar direction to the Loa: There has always been war and while its all fun and games to them, it rarely makes a difference. Borders change, people die, but thats about it, they themselves go unaffected by it. Sure, Tezcatlipoca would delight spreading misfortune through all and every rank and Huizilopochtli almost certainly was a soldier at one point or another to fuel his bloodlust, but whats war to the others? Apart from Tlazolteotl to play the part of a Joy Division member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:15:43-08:00","id":768690,"title":"","content":"There's also the very real possibility that Scions would have completely altered the world by being in the war.<br /> <br /> Think about it. Let's say a Scion of, say, Horus, happens to be a patriotic English citizen who decides to enter the war and use his god-given abilities to smash Nazi faces. Horus may not be all that bothered by it, letting his kid do as he pleases as long as he's still towing the pantheon line.<br /> <br /> Right up until in some pocket realm he ends up getting completely owned by a daughter of Heimdall, at which point Horus yells &quot;Get your hands off my kid!&quot; and intervenes. And the next thing you know the Pesedjet have to follow after Heimdall retaliates, and all of a sudden the Pesedjet are less a curious, mostly uninterested party guarding their own back yard and actively involved as they and the Aesir spit at each other.<br /> <br /> In a world wide war setting it's likely less the gods themselves who will decide policy and, likely, more their kids who follow their human leanings, prejudices, and loyalties who start stuff that their godly parents are going to be obliged to finish because they don't want to look like they're backing down to anyone. Which doesn't mean some of those kids aren't going to be made to pay for it later, but by then lines are probably well and truly drawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}